{
  "query": "At Crestline Media you must right size a new Cloud SQL instance using observed performance and planned growth. Current peaks average 4200 queries per second, 2.5 TB of data, 8000 simultaneous connections and 200 GB of backup usage. The business projects a 60% rise in traffic and a 25% increase in stored data within the next 12 months. Which instance configuration will support the forecast while keeping costs efficient?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "db-n2-standard-32 with 6 TB of HDD storage",
      "explanation": "This uses a standard memory machine type with 32 vCPUs and lower cost HDD persistent disks that prioritize capacity over performance",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "db-n2-highmem-32 with 4 TB of SSD storage",
      "explanation": "This uses a high memory 32 vCPU machine with SSD persistent disks sized to cover the expected data volume and provide strong IOPS",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "db-n2-highmem-64 with 6 TB of SSD storage",
      "explanation": "This provides a high memory 64 vCPU machine and larger SSD capacity that offers substantial headroom for compute and storage",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "db-n2-highmem-16 with 3 TB of SSD storage",
      "explanation": "This is a high memory 16 vCPU machine with SSD storage that favors lower cost but with reduced compute and capacity",
      "correct": false,
